 # Brick-based structures
-    Also called: None.
-    ## Overview
-    Brick-based structures replace the variable-resolution hierarchical subdivision of sparse voxel octrees with fixed-size cubic blocks ("bricks") to optimize for hardware-friendly memory access and parallel construction [Sparse Voxel Brick Set](11886-sparse-voxel-brick-set.md). They solve the traversal complexity and shader divergence of recursive tree structures by enabling branch-free, linear memory access patterns suitable for real-time ray tracing and GPU cache coherency [Brick Map](21177-brick-map.md).
